+
+## 14. Conversation list
+
+### conversation_list
+
+| Field                        | Type                  | Description                                           |
+| ---------------------------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`                       | string                | `"conversation_list"`                                 |
+| `conversations`              | ConversationSummary[] | One page in newest-activity-first order               |
+| `conversations[].sessionId`  | string                | Id usable with the existing `?sessionId=` resume path |
+| `conversations[].createdAt`  | string                | Creation time as an ISO date string                   |
+| `conversations[].updatedAt`  | string                | Activity time as an ISO date string                   |
+| `conversations[].entryCount` | integer               | Number of stored entries                              |
+
+A list is answered only when asked, never pushed, and has no `stream_end`; a request during a running user turn does not wait on that turn's lock ([validated by: answers history before an active user turn ends without taking the session lock](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L301)).
+
+**GDPR.** `conversation_list` carries one authenticated user's own conversation metadata and no conversation content or credentials; the user id comes from the connection, never from the frame, including when a frame carries another user's id ([validated by: lists only the authenticated user, pages tied activity and resumes a listed conversation](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L187)).
+
+`transport.history` is the deployer's independent decision to make that metadata reachable from a client, defaulting off; off or unavailable history returns `UNSUPPORTED`, and store failures return a sanitised `SERVER_ERROR` while leaving the socket open ([validated by: refuses disabled or unavailable history and contains real store failures without closing the socket](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L236)).
+
+Retention remains the consumer's decision under [#41](https://github.com/re-cinq/HALEngine/issues/41), as for resume; see the [conversation-list spec](../hal-engine-conversation-list/spec.md#websocket-history-144).
